{"ld": 1321, "paper": "HP856", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Reform Net Energy Billing by Establishing Limitations on the Programs' Duration and Compensation", "sponsor_id": "h-foster-steven", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bradstreet-richard", "h-faulkingham-william", "s-harrington-matthew", "h-mcintyre-mathew", "h-paul-reagan", "s-stewart-harold", "h-wadsworth-nathan"], "committee_code": "EUT", "committee_name": "Energy, Utilities and Technology", "summary": {"text": "This bill does the following.\n\n1. It amends the law governing the kilowatt-hour credit net energy billing program to provide that, unless a distributed generation resource has met the timing requirements established for participation in the program, only distributed generation resources with a nameplate capacity of 20 kilowatts or less may be used for net energy billing. For distributed generation resources participating pursuant to this provision, the number of shared financial interest customers or meters is limited to 10 and a customer may not, at one time, have a financial interest in more than 5 distributed generation resources that have net energy billing arrangements. The bill also provides that kilowatt-hour credits may be credited only to a customer's electricity supply charges.\n\n2. It amends the law governing the tariff rate net energy billing program to limit the tariff rate to the supply rate of the standard-offer service rate.\n\n3. It amends the laws governing the tariff rate and kilowatt-hour credit net energy billing programs to prohibit participation 20 years from the date a net energy billing agreement between the entity proposing the development of the distributed generation resource and the transmission and distribution utility was executed or on December 31, 2045, whichever occurs earlier. The bill also requires a distributed generation resource participating in net energy billing programs to sell in the State renewable energy credits generated by the resource.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0856&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Accepted Majority (ONTP) Report", "final_disposition": {"label": "Accepted Majority (ONTP) Report", "date": "2025-06-13", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1321)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0856&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-675)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0856&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (H-675)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": null, "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0856&item=2&snum=132", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN132102.pdf"}], "committee_actions": [{"date": "2025-05-29", "action": "Work Session Held", "result": null}, {"date": "2025-05-29", "action": "Voted", "result": "Divided Report"}, {"date": "2025-06-12", "action": "Reported Out", "result": "ONTP/OTP-AM"}], "committee_reports": [{"label": "Majority report", "recommendation": "Ought Not To Pass", "signer_count": 8, "signers": ["Senator Mark Lawrence (Chair)", "Representative Melanie Sachs (Chair)", "Representative Valli Geiger", "Senator Nicole Grohoski", "Representative Christopher Kessler", "Representative Walter Runte", "Representative Sophia Warren", "Representative Kilton Webb"], "signer_ids": ["s-lawrence-mark", "h-sachs-melanie", "h-geiger-valli", "s-grohoski-nicole", "h-kessler-christopher", "h-runte-walter", "h-warren-sophia", "h-webb-kilton"]}, {"label": "Minority report", "recommendation": "Ought To Pass As Amended", "signer_count": 5, "signers": ["Representative Steven Foster", "Senator Matthew Harrington", "Representative Mathew McIntyre", "Representative Reagan Paul", "Representative Nathan Wadsworth